I've carefully reviewed your code and identified the root cause of the map display issue. The problem is with the timing and initialization of Leaflet Geoman - it's trying to load before Leaflet core is fully ready, and the map container dimensions aren't being properly respected.

Here's the simple reliable fix:

The Problem

Your map fails to load because:

1. Leaflet Geoman is being initialized before Leaflet core has fully loaded
2. The map container sometimes has zero height when initialized (hidden tabs)
3. The map.invalidateSize() call isn't being triggered at the right time

The Fix - 3 Easy Steps

Step 1: Update the Map Initialization Code

Find the initMap: function() in your JavaScript (around line 1850). Replace the entire function with this updated version:

```javascript
initMap: function() {
